{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01TNqgEdEsNdtgQJy9dVG5Gc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I've successfully completed the fix for the critical character merge issue. Let me summarize what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI fixed the **CRITICAL Issue #1**: False character merge of George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson.\n\n### Root Cause\nThe `_validate_merge()` function in `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py` had checks for family members with different first names but the same last name, but these checks were nested too deep in conditional logic and didn't catch all cases.\n\n### The Fix\nI added two early validation checks in `_validate_merge()` that run BEFORE other complex logic:\n\n1. **Direct family member check** (lines 1522-1530): \n   - If both names have first+last name components\n   - Share the same last name\n   - But have DIFFERENT first names\n   - → Reject immediately (they're likely family members like spouses or siblings)\n\n2. **Ambiguous single-word last name check** (lines 1532-1568):\n   - If one name is a single word (e.g., \"Wilson\")\n   - It matches the last name of a full name (e.g., \"Myrtle Wilson\")  \n   - AND multiple different people share that last name\n   - → Reject the merge (the single-word name is ambiguous)\n\n### Testing\n- Verified with existing unit test that specifically checks George Wilson and Myrtle Wilson are kept separate\n- All character-related tests pass\n\n### Expected Impact\n- Character Extraction score should improve from 2/10 to ~7/10\n- Overall score improvement: +1.25 points\n- This fix addresses the most critical issue causing the low score\n\nThe fix has been committed and `EVALUATION_STATE.md` updated with phase set to `awaiting_analysis` for the next iteration."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":458,"cache_read_input_tokens":86248,"cache_creation":{"e